[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Independent assertion, artifact and charge audit contracts

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-ASSERT-FINITE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Nonfinite measured values remain indeterminate
STATEMENT: >>>
A missing or nonfinite measurement shall be Indeterminate even when both
assertion bounds are valid finite numbers. Valid inclusive endpoints shall
pass and finite out-of-range values shall fail.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: analyses nonfinite_measurements_are_indeterminate_even_with_valid_finite_bounds.
Implementation: assertion.rs within. NaN and both signed infinities are distinct cases.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-AUDIT-FINITE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Each measured audit operand must be valid
STATEMENT: >>>
A measured physical check shall require a finite discrepancy and a finite
nonnegative tolerance independently. Invalid input shall fail with a reason,
and invalid numeric fields shall serialize as null rather than passing or
producing nonfinite JSON numbers.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: consistency measured_check_requires_each_finite_operand_and_nonnegative_tolerance.
Implementation: audit.rs Check::measured. Finite passing and failing controls retained.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-ARTIFACT-INTEGRITY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Length and digest are independent integrity conditions
STATEMENT: >>>
Verified artifact reads shall reject either a payload length mismatch or a
SHA256 mismatch independently, including valid JSON tampered without changing
length and valid unchanged payloads with an incorrect declared byte count.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: storage_power payload_length_and_digest_are_independent_integrity_requirements.
Implementation: artifact.rs read_verified. A checksum does not authenticate an untrusted author.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: EPOCH-MOS-CHARGE-AUDIT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Independent deep-accumulation terminal KCL
STATEMENT: >>>
For the bounded MOS1 deep-accumulation fixture, intrinsic gate-bulk displacement
shall obey I=Cox*deltaV/h with opposite gate and bulk terminal currents. The
audit shall preserve this result under a common-mode voltage translation and
scale the relative KCL tolerance by the sum of absolute terminal currents.
A deliberately perturbed supplying current shall fail the gate KCL check.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification: consistency accumulation_mos_charge_audit_matches_independent_capacitor_and_common_mode.
Manufactured states use three voltage steps, three time steps and three offsets without calling the
production capacitance routine for expected values. This finite accumulation
fixture does not qualify inversion, native BSIM providers or arbitrary device behavior.
<<<
